    "issuer": "Shanghai Municipal Commission of Housing and Urban-Rural Development / municipal historic building protection centre, relayed by Shanghai Fabu and Jing’an government",
    "summary": "The institution describes a 1920 semi-detached three-storey brick-and-timber garden house, two projecting southern gables, central veranda and curved ends, and notes that the bookshop on the street and the iron gate leading to the foundation are separate entrances. The gate and the modern green glass storefront also appear independently in the 2015 curb photographs. The north-facing ochre window wing in the garden is identified from matched roof, parapet, return, two distinct apertures and the adjacent right-hand projection; its construction date is unspecified. The 1920 date is not attached to this individual appendage.",
